SUMMARY:Heal Emotional Bad Habits for the Good Life You Prefer 
DESCRIPTION:Raleigh & Triangle Activities Meetup Group\nYes\, you have a c
 odependent relationship with negativity that results in emotional bad habi
 ts that destroy your life. So what? Everyone has that stuff on Earth! This
  is a very polarized planet\, which can inspire tremendously positive pers
 onal growth. Or not\, if you choose to remain ignorant and follow bad lead
 ers. What you need is learn to recognize and handle you own monster potent
 ials so you can live happy ever after. Or don’t\, and remain a wreck. Ei
 ther way you won’t be lacking for company! If there’s one thing Earth 
 is good at\, it’s an abundance of whatever you expect to experience. So 
 rest assured that whichever you favor-- miracles or misery -- the choice i
 s so easy that you didn’t know you were already choosing it.\n\nJoin us 
 this Sunday Sep 27\, 2026 for a free liberating talk on how to change the 
 habits that are killing you. We’re adults here\, right? We can talk abou
 t current splitting realities without getting paranoid\, dramatic\, or def
 ensively denying. Earth is on the brink of death or rebirth because the cy
 cles are coming to a close. That’s just how nature must work\, since you
  are an eternal consciousness. Folks who insist on remaining unconscious w
 ill experience an unconscious continuation of life\, which means they die 
 and then find out the truth. “Aww shucks\, there’s an afterlife after 
 all! I guess I didn’t have to live so fearfully.”\n\nSo even if you do
 n’t know how life really works\, you might want to consider Pascal’s w
 ager. In the 1600’s French philosopher Blaise Pascal said look\, it’s 
 worth it to give God a chance to exist. If you’re atheist and wrong\, th
 en by opposing God you may have wrecked your own eternity. But if you’re
  theist and wrong\, then believing in a God that doesn’t exist doesn’t
  lose much\, just some idealism and charitable living. So what kind of gam
 bler are you? Of course\, we miss the point if by trying to please God the
 n we join an obnoxious society that encourages toxic addictive behaviors l
 ike judgmentalism. Most religions start with someone nice like Jesus who m
 akes great suggestions for better living\, then rude people take over to j
 ustify their inner monster. As Shakespeare said\, “The devil can quote s
 criptures for his own purposes.”\n\nFortunately\, with Earth 1.0 coming 
 to a close we get plenty of lifestyle examples to draw upon for confident 
 conclusions. Like the Dalai Lama says\, “If you can’t help people\, at
  least don’t hurt them.” And yet so many people choose to hurt each ot
 her! Why? Some folks like to say that humanity is evil and should be destr
 oyed. Presumably they’ll enjoy their judgmentalism until the Earth dies 
 with them on it. Don’t worry though\, you don’t have to join them if y
 ou change your own bad habits. Reality is a multiverse with endless parall
 el Earths that survive and thrive. It’s just how higher dimensions work\
 , with every branching possibility existing before the timeline that your 
 current life story lands you in. The more you examine your habitual lifest
 yle choices\, the more you can change your whole life “just in time”.\
 n\nThe more charitable view of humanity is that everyone is just doing the
  best they can. Be kind\, you don’t know what burdens people carry. Ok\,
  but I say people just do the best they think they can. You can always do 
 better if you think you can\, and you can’t do what you think is impossi
 ble. This is your power to choose beliefs. Positive beliefs support you in
  always becoming a better person on your own happy ever after timeline. Ne
 gative beliefs make you think you’re always failing\, so you struggle\, 
 suffer\, react badly\, and become your own worst enemy. God is the directi
 on of eternal positive life energy. The devil is your inner monster that p
 ushes for the worst habits to wreck your life. Either way you get lots of 
 company\, so living in heaven or hell is up to you.\n\nFor this meetup\, m
 ake a list of habits that you think are bad and need to change. Review the
  list to feel the deeper judgments going on. After all\, what matters in l
 ife isn’t what you have\, it’s how you use it. Positive energy makes y
 ou feel positive and hopeful\, negative makes you feel negative and hopele
 ss. You’ll see how life really works with your own higher plans to incar
 nate on Earth for lessons in loving self-creatorship. We’ll review commo
 n negative choice patterns in human society\, and see how easy habits are 
 to change with self-acceptance for the self-esteem that inherits more divi
 ne self-worth. We conclude with a guided meditation to forgive and replace
  old habits with new joys of working with your higher self and soul family
 .\n\nWelcome! Our Inner Selves Mastery spiritual support group is free onl
 ine every Sunday 11am-130pm EDT\, with the last 30 minutes for a guided me
 ditation. If you can’t stay you can get the recording. You can signup he
 re for this meeting and visit www.signupISM.com for all events\, newslette
 r\, videos\, and more.\n\nBest wishes\,\nCarl Johann Schroeder\nInner Selv
 es Mastery\nspiritual teaching and coaching\nquick-links at [www.signupISM
 .com](http://www.signupISM.com)
